% ceo-performance-award.l4: the history view
%
% The timeless Logical English twin of the contracts of an L4 file (ceo-performance-award.l4), written
% by the L4 translator (docs/migration/l4.md, step 3): the contracts read over a finished
% history of events. For each obligation the program says when it starts, its deadline
% and which events meet it, and four rules say how it ends: met, missed, or still
% open when the history stops. The same obligations, in the same words, as the LE for LPS twin in LPS2's
% examples/migration/l4/; each scenario expects what that twin's run ended with, which
% agrees with L4's evaluator.
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program was written by a translator from a program of another
% system. It is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
% implied, including any warranty that it is accurate, complete or fit for a
% particular purpose. The translation may be wrong: check it against its source
% before relying on it. It is not legal, tax, insurance, financial or other
% professional advice. Its authors accept no liability for any loss or damage
% arising from its use.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    something happens on day *a day*.
    an obligation can start on day *a day*.
    the contract eligible service requirement starts on day *a day* with award state *an award state*; scenario element.
    the termination reason of *a ceo award state* is *a value*.
    the musk service status of *a ceo award state* is *a value*.
    the value of seventh and half anniversary is *a value*; memorable.
    the value of grant date is *a value*; memorable.
    the value of trillion for value *a value* is *a value input*; memorable.
    the value of billion for value *a value* is *a value input*; memorable.
    the value of million for value *a value* is *a value input*; memorable.
    the last closing price of *a tesla performance metrics* is *a value*.
    the per share consideration of *a tesla performance metrics* is *a value*.
    the performance metrics of *a ceo award state* is *a value*.
    the earned tranches of *a ceo award state* is *a value*.
    the value of fifth anniversary is *a value*; memorable.
    the ceo succession framework of *a ceo award state* is *a value*.
    the covered event occurred of *a ceo award state* is *a value*.
    the covered event type of *a ceo award state* is *a value*.
    the hsr waiting period expired of *a ceo award state* is *a value*.
    the shareholder approval received of *a ceo award state* is *a value*.
    the current date of *a ceo award state* is *a value*.
    the value of performance end date is *a value*; memorable.
    the value of performance period years is *a value*; memorable.
    the contract milestone achievement requirement starts on day *a day* with tranche *a tranche* and award state *an award state*; scenario element.
    the value of required market cap for tranche for tranche number *a tranche number* is *a value*; memorable.
    the contract vesting requirement starts on day *a day* with tranche *a tranche* and award state *an award state*; scenario element.

